/-!
# Collective agency

Temporary coalitions combine voluntary participation, persistent knowledge,
witnessed commitments and revocable authority. The lifecycle has independent
source rules and a two-sided typed GSLT realization. Exact authority queries
remain separate from approximate numeric decision scores.

The inference hive executes two complete episodes. The spatial swarm uses
linear resources for occupancy, with checked actuation, conservation,
collision freedom and explicit reachability obstructions. A subordinate
certified journal supplies agreement and durable-prefix safety, together with
conditional finite-quorum progress; it is not a general live consensus protocol.

Knowledge, consent, authority, factual truth and physical compliance are
different obligations throughout these interfaces.
-/
